    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n102763" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέγεος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέγος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>at</i> or <i>near the roof</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ.
				θάλαμοι</span>, of the women's chambers, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπερῷον</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				6.248
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>roofed</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διὸς τ. δόμοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Emp.
					142
				</span></i>
			, and so perh. in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i> l.c., though <i><span class="en">
				Apollon.
				<u>Lex.</u>
			</span></i> glosses by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπερῷοι</span>.</div>
